### TopUp Wallet — Auth.Api
### Issues JWT access + refresh tokens. Stateless: nothing stored, tokens are
### self-expiring and validated by signature. Log in, then call the wallet/topup
### APIs with the access token as a Bearer header.
###
### DEMO credential rule: any non-empty username + password succeeds (real user
### management / Auth0 is out of scope). The username becomes the token subject.

@auth = http://localhost:5003
@contentType = application/json

### Health
GET {{auth}}/health

###
# @name login
### Log in. Returns { accessToken, refreshToken, tokenType, expiresInSeconds }.
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "alice",
  "password": "any-non-empty"
}

###
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.$.refreshToken}}

### Who am I (needs the ACCESS token)
GET {{auth}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Refresh — exchange the refresh token for a NEW access + refresh pair.
POST {{auth}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Empty credentials -> 400
POST {{auth}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "username": "",
  "password": ""
}

### A refresh token must NOT work as an access token -> 401
GET {{auth}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshToken}}
